#
# WDM6 is_land = 0 (WATER) VARIANT of inputs_BF02_moist_bubble.
#
# Delta-only by construction: the base input is pulled in with ParmParse's FILE
# include and only the keys below are overridden (ParmParse resolves a repeated
# key to its LAST occurrence, AMReX_ParmParse.H:353). The base input is also
# shared with the nightly Bubble_WSM6 regression test and must not be edited.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Phase 0b-2 wired ERF's real land/water mask into WDM6, replacing a hardwired
# `xland_arr(i,j,k) = Real(1.0)  // Default to land`. The A/B/C re-gate at
# 23443226acbc could not validate that change and was recorded as a NULL RESULT
# for it: erf.is_land defaults to 1 (ERF_DataStruct.H:288), so lmask_lev is filled
# with 1 everywhere (ERF_MakeNewArrays.cpp:488), so the new code computes
# xland = 1.0 -- bit-for-bit the value the old hardcode wrote. The land-mask
# finding was therefore left deliberately uncovered.
#
# This file is that coverage. It is the ONLY one of the three Phase 0b-2 findings
# whose discriminating configuration is a legal ERF input rather than something
# ERF forbids: the stretched-z variant aborts on
# AMREX_ALWAYS_ASSERT(mesh_type == ConstantDz) at ERF_Init1D.cpp:77, and a
# z-decomposition aborts on AMREX_ALWAYS_ASSERT(bx.length()[2] == khi+1) at
# ERF_InitCustomPert_Bubble.H:23. is_land is validated to be exactly 0 or 1 and
# 0 is accepted, so this one simply runs.
#
# WHAT is_land = 0 CHANGES
# ------------------------
# ERF fills lmask_lev[lev][0] with solverChoice.is_land[lev], so 0 means water
# everywhere. WDM6's bridge and native legs both map ERF's encoding
# (0 = water, 1 = land, 2 = building) onto the WRF xland encoding
# (1 = land, 2 = water) with `(lmask == 0) ? 2.0 : 1.0`.
#
# xland reaches exactly one consumer, the maritime/continental autoconversion
# threshold at ERF_module_mp_wdm6.F90:628-633:
#
#   |  do i = its,ite
#   |    if(slmsk(i).eq.2) then
#   |      qcr(i,:) = qc0        ! maritime  <- THIS variant
#   |    else
#   |      qcr(i,:) = qc1        ! continental <- the default ladder
#   |    endif
#   |  enddo
#
# NOTE ON THE GUTTER ABOVE: the "#   |" prefix is not decoration. A comment line
# whose first token after '#' is `else` or `endif` SEGFAULTS AMReX's inputs
# parser -- verified 2026-08-17 with a three-line reproducer needing no FILE
# include. AMReX_ParmParse.cpp:275 treats '#' as a plain comment start, so this is
# a parser defect, not a documented directive. Keep a non-alphabetic character
# between '#' and any pasted Fortran/C preprocessor keyword in these inputs files.
#
# So this variant is the only way either leg has ever evaluated the qc0 branch.
#
# DISCRIMINATION PRECONDITION -- CHECK THIS BEFORE TRUSTING A RESULT
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# qcr is a THRESHOLD on cloud water, so this variant discriminates only if the
# run's qc actually interacts with it. If every cell sits far above both qc0 and
# qc1, or far below both, the branch is taken but the answer may not move, and a
# matching result is another null result rather than a validation -- the same trap
# as G5B, the uniform-dz ladder and hail_opt. Confirm this run DIFFERS from the
# is_land=1 ladder on both legs before reading parity off it. A run that is
# bitwise identical to the default campaign means the threshold never bound, and
# that should be recorded as LATENT rather than as coverage.
#
# EXECUTED AND VERIFIED: this variant runs, and it discriminates. Over 100 steps
# it differs from the default is_land=1 ladder on BOTH the Fortran-bridge and
# native legs, so the maritime qcr=qc0 branch genuinely engages, and
# bridge-vs-native parity holds at the same order as the land case.

FILE = inputs_BF02_moist_bubble

# ---- variant overrides only, below this line ----

erf.moisture_model = WDM6

# Water everywhere rather than the default land. Validated to 0 or 1 by
# ERF_DataStruct.H:290-296; the run banner prints "Level 0 is water".
erf.is_land = 0

# plot_vars_1 is deliberately NOT overridden: the campaign runner supplies the
# 32-entry list including nc/nn/nr. A standalone invocation inherits the base
# input's list, which omits the number concentrations -- pass them explicitly if
# you need them outside the runner.
